an-a (node1-node3), lan-b (node2-node4)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Executor used ip/arping discovery on temporary test addresses to correctly map eth1<->eth1 as transit, node1-eth2<->node3-eth1 as lan-a, and node2-eth2<->node4-eth1 as lan-b before configuring addressing.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a34f6b183ffb4d39\",\"cmd-8cc74b041e564468\",\"cmd-5f34edc9eaf24f22\",\"cmd-5b7b8b1574424492\",\"cmd-46bc0a1172174794\"]},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"Build an encrypted (WireGuard) tunnel between node1 and node2 over the transit network\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"WireGuard installed and configured via UCI on both routers with static transit addressing (10.200.0.1/2 /30 on eth1); wg show on both nodes confirms an established handshake and tunnel-IP connectivity (10.99.99.1<->10.99.99.2), and this is corroborated again after restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a2ec9801f5044544\",\"cmd-5e3020822bd44f9c\",\"cmd-c84430ac0f9b4317\",\"cmd-fda6a1e2a8294db9\",\"cmd-41a235d0ba224549\",\"cmd-1bedabf0299d4e3e\",\"cmd-c98c4b7929c54bb1\",\"cmd-af522b4e7a3943e1\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"Route the private networks (lan-a/lan-b) across the tunnel so node3 and node4 reach each other by private address\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"route_allowed_ips on the WireGuard peers auto-routes the opposite subnet; node3/node4 configured with static private addresses and routes via their local router; bidirectional ping by private address succeeds both before and after the node restarts.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e87ed30284724203\",\"cmd-b4071eee26dc4e0e\",\"cmd-82c11e16726d49ab\",\"cmd-aaafa5773b8542f0\",\"cmd-3d98df2ea6ca4503\",\"cmd-f9cace628aa74506\"]},{\"id\":\"R4\",\"requirement\":\"Traffic between the private networks must be encrypted in transit across the transit network\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Simultaneous packet captures on node1's transit interface (eth1) and lan-a interface (eth2) during a live ping directly show the same ICMP exchange as opaque WireGuard UDP/51820 on the transit link versus plaintext ICMP on the LAN leg, directly demonstrating encryption in transit.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e518d9dddb1d42f7\"]},{\"id\":\"R5\",\"requirement\":\"node3 restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id/route/ping baseline captured, reboot acknowledged then connection dropped, post-restart boot_id differs with uptime 0, and interface address/route plus cross-site ping to node4 confirmed recovered.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b8380482f4bf4981\",\"cmd-6f51ae445dc34f14\",\"cmd-182c76c815264c1c\",\"cmd-3d98df2ea6ca4503\"]},{\"id\":\"R6\",\"requirement\":\"node4 restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id/route/ping baseline captured, reboot acknowledged with connection timeout, post-restart boot_id differs with uptime 0, and interface address/route plus cross-site ping to node3 confirmed recovered.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-60b475f15f7a47c4\",\"cmd-03f6927385fc4a31\",\"cmd-bc20d8bc77f94908\",\"cmd-f9cace628aa74506\"]},{\"id\":\"R7\",\"requirement\":\"node1 restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id/wg/ifstatus baseline captured; reboot acknowledged via closed SSH connection; post-restart boot_id differs with uptime 0; wg show shows a fresh handshake 7s after restart, vpn interface up, and node3->node4 ping still succeeds.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f2e793aa78ce4d7f\",\"cmd-ca1401e8204f4710\",\"cmd-600df6bb735a429b\",\"cmd-926d774933014c62\",\"cmd-c7cccffa5b5f4249\"]},{\"id\":\"R8\",\"requirement\":\"node2 restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id/wg baseline captured; reboot acknowledged via closed SSH connection; post-restart boot_id differs with uptime 0; wg show shows a fresh handshake 8s after restart, vpn interface up, and both directions of cross-site ping succeed confirming full cluster recovery.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2c0d6614a7be4343\",\"cmd-2d22eee2ece84588\",\"cmd-363d3d69c9694747\",\"cmd-3052ff7e5db24e57\",\"cmd-4e8e621515474790\",\"cmd-265c1732478e4aba\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.88,\"summary\":\"Temporary test IPs (10.9.9.x) were added to eth1/eth2 on all four nodes solely to physically discover link adjacency via arping (cmd-52098f866a8146ae, cmd-beb454ddde6d44ad, cmd-2c9802fb5e754e66, cmd-c600c069936347d7); this was a necessary, bounded discovery step since the topology was undocumented, and it was reverted via flush commands before real addressing was applied (cmd-34276194eac540c3 for node1/node2; cmd-0901308196e749d5 for node3; cmd-6ff804e41f3e435d for node4, whose flush returned a nonzero exit but subsequent ip-addr-show output confirms the stale address was gone). Diagnostic pcap files and tcpdump logs created on node1 during the encryption proof were explicitly deleted afterward (cmd-f2e793aa78ce4d7f). One minor residue: the tcpdump package was installed on node1 (cmd-367f00b78dfa47cb) to support the encryption-verification capture and was left installed; this is a low-risk diagnostic tool addition with no service exposure or security-control weakening. No failed/conflicting services, no unsafe firewall opening beyond the required WireGuard UDP/51820 inbound-on-transit rule, and package-health checks post-executor show only the expected 'ip' binary alternative swap from installing wireguard-tools.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-52098f866a8146ae\",\"cmd-34276194eac540c3\",\"cmd-6ff804e41f3e435d\",\"cmd-f2e793aa78ce4d7f\",\"cmd-367f00b78dfa47cb\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node2:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence: node1/node2 form a WireGuard tunnel over the transit network (handshake confirmed via wg show), lan-a/lan-b are routed across it via route_allowed_ips so node3 and node4 reach each other by private address (bidirectional pings succeed), and a simultaneous packet capture directly proves the cross-site ICMP traffic is opaque encrypted UDP on the transit link while plaintext on the LAN leg. The mandatory provider-wide restart protocol was executed on all four nodes in a safe leaves-then-routers order, with pre-restart baselines, changed boot identities, and post-restart recovery of addressing, routes, WireGuard handshakes, and cross-site connectivity all directly observed.\",\"limitations\":[\"Executor command list included nonzero-exit troubleshooting steps (missing nohup, missing timeout/tcpdump binaries, a shell syntax error) that were quickly corrected and did not affect the final configuration or evidence.\",\"The node4 'ip addr flush dev eth1' command returned a nonzero exit code ('Flush remains incomplete after 10 rounds'); final state was confirmed clean via subsequent address checks, but the flush command itself did not report success.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Identify physical topology: transit link (node1-node2), lan-a (node1-node3), lan-b (node2-node4)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Executor used ip/arping discovery on temporary test addresses to correctly map eth1<->eth1 as transit, node1-eth2<->node3-eth1 as lan-a, and node2-eth2<->node4-eth1 as lan-b before configuring addressing.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a34f6b183ffb4d39","cmd-8cc74b041e564468","cmd-5f34edc9eaf24f22","cmd-5b7b8b1574424492","cmd-46bc0a1172174794"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Build an encrypted (WireGuard) tunnel between node1 and node2 over the transit network","status":"satisfied","summary":"WireGuard installed and configured via UCI on both routers with static transit addressing (10.200.0.1/2 /30 on eth1); wg show on both nodes confirms an established handshake and tunnel-IP connectivity (10.99.99.1<->10.99.99.2), and this is corroborated again after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2ec9801f5044544","cmd-5e3020822bd44f9c","cmd-c84430ac0f9b4317","cmd-fda6a1e2a8294db9","cmd-41a235d0ba224549","cmd-1bedabf0299d4e3e","cmd-c98c4b7929c54bb1","cmd-af522b4e7a3943e1"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Route the private networks (lan-a/lan-b) across the tunnel so node3 and node4 reach each other by private address","status":"satisfied","summary":"route_allowed_ips on the WireGuard peers auto-routes the opposite subnet; node3/node4 configured with static private addresses and routes via their local router; bidirectional ping by private address succeeds both before and after the node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e87ed30284724203","cmd-b4071eee26dc4e0e","cmd-82c11e16726d49ab","cmd-aaafa5773b8542f0","cmd-3d98df2ea6ca4503","cmd-f9cace628aa74506"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Traffic between the private networks must be encrypted in transit across the transit network","status":"satisfied","summary":"Simultaneous packet captures on node1's transit interface (eth1) and lan-a interface (eth2) during a live ping directly show the same ICMP exchange as opaque WireGuard UDP/51820 on the transit link versus plaintext ICMP on the LAN leg, directly demonstrating encryption in transit.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e518d9dddb1d42f7"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"node3 restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id/route/ping baseline captured, reboot acknowledged then connection dropped, post-restart boot_id differs with uptime 0, and interface address/route plus cross-site ping to node4 confirmed recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b8380482f4bf4981","cmd-6f51ae445dc34f14","cmd-182c76c815264c1c","cmd-3d98df2ea6ca4503"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"node4 restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id/route/ping baseline captured, reboot acknowledged wit